{
 "header": [
  "SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0",
  "Copyright (C) 2026 Artur Andrzejczak <andrzejczak.artur@gmail.com>",
  "",
  "ISP overrides for the OV5647 NoIR module (no infrared cut filter) on",
  "L4T R32 and R35, for LED light. Fitted to a ColorChecker on raw",
  "frames from two modules under three LED sources, and checked on the",
  "ISP output of a Nano (R32) and a Xavier NX (R35). Generated by",
  "tools/isp/make-override.py from camera_overrides_noir.json. See",
  "docs/isp-tuning.md. Not for daylight, see the Outdoors section there.",
  "",
  "The white points are the mean of two modules. The modules differ by",
  "about 3% in R/G and 6% in B/G. Slot 5 and the 8500 K set repeat",
  "source C, with its matrix as fitted. The other LED matrices have a",
  "saturation of 1.2 folded in.",
  "",
  "Install:",
  "  sudo cp camera_overrides_noir.isp /var/nvidia/nvcam/settings/camera_overrides.isp",
  "  sudo chmod 664 /var/nvidia/nvcam/settings/camera_overrides.isp",
  "  sudo rm -f /var/nvidia/nvcam/settings/nvcam_cache_*.bin",
  "  sudo systemctl restart nvargus-daemon",
  "A line Argus rejects stops the camera, and journalctl -u nvargus-daemon",
  "names it."
 ],
